WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.020
I think it started from young...

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.600
I watched a lot of cartoons from Japan.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.040
You had your "Gatchaman", "Captain Future" and "Transformers".

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:24.280
Whenever I look at my toys in my cabinets, I will think about all my childhood memories;

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:29.440
like how I used to save up money and run to the shop and purchase it.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.740
I would take it out the box and just play with it with my friends.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:38.020
Hi! My name is Simon Sim, I'm 49 years old and I'm a professional photographer.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.320
I've been collecting toys for about 20 years.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.100
My recent collection would be Kaiju Sofubi.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.040
They are mainly from Japan, but there are some from the US and UK as well.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:04.160
I would go to Japan once a year and try to get Kaijus there.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:10.160
I try to make it for their toy conventions if possible, if not I'll get them from the stores.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:20.380
Japanese they are very creative in their own ways and I find their culture is something I appreciate...

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.960
The Japanese people can really think out of the box

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.500
and they create all these funny-looking figures that I can't see anywhere else.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:31.340
My collection consists of many various makers and brands like...

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.480
Bearbricks, Transformers, 3A from Hong Kong,

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.900
KAWS, Chogokin.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.480
One of my favourite animation movie is 'Akira'.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:41.300
I have the motorcycle from the movie.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.920
I also have modular LEGO,

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.520
As well as Kaijus from Japan!

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:53.680
I did collect a few Kaijus before this but this particular piece is what made me go hardcore.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.700
The one that makes these toys is Hirota Saigansho.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.980
and he makes his own toys. [Sofubi]

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.700
So these are all handmade from his factory

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:03.880
and you can only get it via lottery.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:07.900
I'm quite lucky that I got this for my first lottery.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.320
It's been my favourite ever since.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.000
I would treasure this for the rest of my life.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.360
This is one of the rare Kaiju.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.800
This is number 1 out of 30 pieces.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.960
'King Gorilla Ju' also from Hirota

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:34.200
I was surprised I actually got #1, as the maker selects who will receive the toy.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.400
Toys made in Japan still have one of the best plastics.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.760
I'm not sure why, I believe they have a special mix in their plastics.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:48.800
The combination is richer, it doesn't get sticky over time, even in the Singapore climate.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:55.280
This is from US, this is MVH a.k.a Mutant Vinyl Hardcore from Mandarake.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:00.520
His real name is Rich and he makes wonderful Kaijus

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:02.080
His paint job is quite nice

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:06.800
and this is one of the rare US toy makers that I follow.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:11.260
Recently, it's getting a lot harder to get into his lottery

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.760
because there are too many collectors are going for his stuff.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.440
People from all around the world are collecting Kaiju Sofubi now.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.520
There are collectors from Taiwan, Thailand, China, Hong Kong

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:29.600
I'm competing with all these people, These toys are limited to only about 30 pieces.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:33.320
It's still affordable, it's about a few hundred dollars, it's still okay for me.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:39.360
The maker will actually list the price of the Kaiju. So if you think you can afford it, you can participate in the lottery.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:43.000
To win a lottery, I think you need to be a bit lucky.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:50.960
I try to keep my toys in my custom built cabinet.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.880
I'll clean it maybe twice a year.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.300
I've been collecting over 20 years

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:03.020
and I don't dare calculate how much I have spent

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:08.520
because I find putting everything in prices will have a different direction for me.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:20.120
I try not to do that, but to estimate maybe...$50,000 for the past 20 years. I think it's reasonable.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:26.880
On Kaijus alone, I have about 200 pieces.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:30.120
I think collectibles are meant to be on display.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.960
It's very sad to see them inside the box and not being able to see all of it.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:36.920
You need to show the uniqueness of the shape and the vibrance of colours.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:41.040
I love to display them, I can have a look any time I want to.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.400
And share with my friends and family.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:50.240
When you come to my place to see my toys, you will discover bits and pieces. You will see something new everytime.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:56.960
I don't stick to a particular collection because I like variety

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.000
and also following a different phase in my life - it's always changing.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.480
It's a changing of my thoughts and perspective.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.520
Now everything is accessible online and very convenient.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:13.560
It's different now, I have the money, I just need to click on the button and buy it!

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:19.560
In a way it lost a bit of that nostalgia from last time.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:28.280
It's sad, but I still have the memories. That's why I started collecting.

